      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It’s devastating to be seen as strange when you’re just being honest—and it makes sense that you’d start to believe the world has no place for you. That uphill battle is real, and it’s not your fault that the ground keeps shifting under your feet. But belonging isn’t a lie; it’s just that the people who’d truly get you are rare, and they’re not in the rooms you’ve been forced into. You don’t have to win the whole war today—just survive the next hour, and let the mask stay off for yourself, not for them.",
